ainted-steel work installed at Hockfield Court near the Stata Center.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/aesops-fables-ii-2005","source_title":"Aesop's Fables, II, 2005 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from the outdoor lawn and respect any on-site barriers or event setup.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-stata-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Ray and Maria Stata Center","title":"Circle the Stata Center exterior","subtitle":"Building 32, northeast MIT campus","notes":"Walk around the outdoor edges of Frank Gehry’s Building 32 and compare its brick, steel, aluminum, and brightly painted forms from different viewpoints.","short_summary":"A named MIT building with deliberately irregular, mixed-material architecture.","evidence_claim":"MIT List identifies the Ray and Maria Stata Center as Frank Gehry’s 2004 Building 32 and describes its steel, brick, aluminum, and painted volumes.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/ray-maria-stata-center-2004","source_title":"Ray and Maria Stata Center, 2004 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Treat this as an exterior stop; enter only areas that are open to visitors.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-sean-collier-memorial","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Sean Collier Memorial","title":"Visit the Sean Collier Memorial","subtitle":"Vassar Street entrance of the Stata Center","notes":"At the Vassar Street entrance, take a quiet moment to observe the granite memorial’s open central passage and read the site as a place of remembrance.","short_summary":"A named public memorial with a passage formed by interdependent granite blocks.","evidence_claim":"MIT List states that the Sean Collier Memorial, at the Stata Center’s Vassar Street entrance, was commissioned to honor Officer Sean Collier.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/sean-collier-memorial-2015","source_title":"Sean Collier Memorial, 2015 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2022-01-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This is an outdoor memorial; maintain a respectful, quiet visit and do not climb on the structure.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-kresge-auditorium","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Kresge Auditorium","title":"Study Kresge’s three-point roof","subtitle":"Building W16, west campus","notes":"Walk to Kresge’s lawn-side exterior and look for the copper roof pulling down at three points; view any performance only with a separately available ticket.","short_summary":"An Eero Saarinen auditorium known for its thin-shell roof geometry.","evidence_claim":"MIT List identifies Kresge Auditorium as Eero Saarinen’s 1955 Building W16 and describes its roof as an eighth segment of a sphere tied to the ground at three points.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/kresge-auditorium-1955","source_title":"Kresge Auditorium, 1955 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the exterior and lawn as the default visit; auditorium entry depends on building and event access.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-chapel","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"MIT Chapel","title":"Find the MIT Chapel’s light well","subtitle":"Building W15, beside Kresge Auditorium","notes":"Cross the quadrangle to view the chapel’s cylindrical brick exterior and surrounding shallow moat; if the building is open, enter quietly and observe posted guidance.","short_summary":"A nondenominational Saarinen chapel designed as an intimate contrast to nearby campus buildings.","evidence_claim":"MIT List identifies the MIT Chapel as Eero Saarinen’s 1954 Building W15 and describes its cylindrical form, shallow moat, and nondenominational purpose.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/mit-chapel-1954","source_title":"MIT Chapel, 1954 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior viewing is appropriate; interior access can vary with services, ceremonies, and building operations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-stratton-student-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Stratton Student Center","title":"Regroup at Stratton Student Center","subtitle":"Building W20, across from Kresge Auditorium","notes":"Use the exterior plaza as a waypoint, then enter only if open to visitors; notice the intersecting stairways and multipurpose layout described by MIT’s art center.","short_summary":"A named student-center building facing the Kresge and Chapel area.","evidence_claim":"MIT List identifies the Stratton Student Center as Building W20 across from Kresge Auditorium and MIT Chapel, with dining and large gathering spaces inside.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/stratton-student-center-1963","source_title":"Stratton Student Center, 1963 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Indoor access and dining availability may vary; use the exterior as a reliable stop and check posted entry information.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-baker-house","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Baker House","title":"Finish beside Baker House","subtitle":"Building W7, Memorial Drive by the Charles River","notes":"End with an exterior walk along Memorial Drive and look at Baker House’s curved river-facing form; respect that it is a residence hall and avoid residential entry.","short_summary":"A riverfront MIT residence hall designed by Alvar Aalto.","evidence_claim":"MIT List identifies Baker House as Alvar Aalto’s 1949 Building W7 and states that more than 90 percent of its student rooms look out onto the Charles River.","source_url":"https://listart.mit.edu/art-artists/baker-house-1949","source_title":"Baker House, 1949 | MIT List Visual Arts Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from public outdoor areas only; this is a student residence hall rather than a visitor interior.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
